@startuml

title ores.storage.api Component

set namespaceSeparator ::

namespace ores #F2F2F2 {
    namespace storage #F2F2F2 {
        namespace net #F2F2F2 {
            class storage_paths <<struct>> {
            }
        }
    }
}

' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads data members and nothing else, so the class arrives
' as an empty box: it is a static-method surface. The block below fills it in
' and gives it the colour the conventions table asks for.

class ores::storage::net::storage_paths <<struct>> #F7E5FF {
    {static} +prefix : string_view
    {static} +make_object_path(bucket : string_view, key : string_view) : string
    {static} +make_object_url(base_url : string_view, bucket : string_view, key : string_view) : string
}
note right of "ores::storage::net::storage_paths"
Header-only. It builds the /api/v1/storage/{bucket}/{key}
shape and nothing else, and it is the one part of the
component the domain libraries call directly: ores.compute
and ores.ore build their own bucket keys with it. The part
is an INTERFACE library, because it has no translation unit.
end note

together {
    class ores::storage::tests::storage_paths_tests <<test suite>> #C5E1A5 {
        +make_object_path_uses_the_storage_api_prefix() : void
        +make_object_url_prepends_the_base_url() : void
        +prefix_matches_the_storage_api_path() : void
        +key_with_slashes_survives_unchanged() : void
    }
    note bottom of "ores::storage::tests::storage_paths_tests"
    The path shape, asserted as exact strings.
    end note
}

ores::storage::tests::storage_paths_tests ..> ores::storage::net::storage_paths : tests

